WEBVTT

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:13.050
Neku Sakuraba!

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:16.260
I can hardly believe that
<i>you </i>were the chosen one.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.480
What do you mean?!

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:29.530
I don't need to explain myself.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.450
Now, disappear.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.300
What?!

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:54.130
Don't go forgettin' about me!

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:00.220
What'd I tell you?

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:03.230
The next Composer is gonna be me!

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:14.900
Don't go trying to fight on your own.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:16.990
We're right here with you.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.120
I'm out of time.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:29.960
Neku.

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:39.800
OK!

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:49.060
Begone!

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:54.070
Come on, Mr. Mew!

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:08.620
I've got an attack with your name on it!

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:16.340
I cannot lose to the likes of you!

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:33.650
Chew on this!

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.580
Sharpen your senses.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:49.790
--Right!
--Got it!

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:42.180
Am I unable to... defend... Shibuya?

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:54.650
This time, we won for sure.

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:56.820
It's not over yet.

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:02.400
Let's meet the Composer.

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:17.130
"The World Ends With You The Animation"

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:40.460
"Final Episode: It's a Wonderful World"

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:42.130
"Final Episode: It's a Wonderful World"
Wow.

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:45.300
Check out this graffiti.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.510
It's CAT's.

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:49.890
Did he do all of this?

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:51.100
That's right.

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:56.390
All of your...

00:05:56.390 --> 00:06:03.360
All of your works always cheered me
on and told me to enjoy life more.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:08.570
That's why I always went to
that place to look at your graffiti.

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:12.780
I had a really great
time just looking at it.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:17.120
I thought I'd finally met
someone I could look up to.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:19.080
So...

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.290
...why did you...?

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:26.470
But I'm done hesitating.

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:31.930
I know you're here, Mr. Hanekoma!

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:35.520
Come out, Composer!

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:43.230
It's been ages, Neku.

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:45.280
Joshua?!

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:47.740
Is it really you?

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.950
That's right.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:53.080
I see you've been working hard.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:55.410
I thought you were dead.

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:58.870
I was able to make it this far
because you covered for me.

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:01.920
Thank you.

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:09.840
And thanks to you,
I was able to win the game.

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:14.050
Yeah. We won the Reapers' Game!

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:15.310
Not quite.

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:16.640
Huh?

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:20.060
We haven't been playing the Reapers' Game.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:23.310
Say what?

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:25.440
Would it make sense if I told you

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:29.240
that Megumi and I have been playing
a game for the fate of Shibuya?

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:34.490
You see, I'm Shibuya's Composer.

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:49.010
This Shibuya is awash in selfish desires.
I've decided to end it.

00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:50.590
End Shibuya?!

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:52.380
But why, Composer?!

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:55.390
Because I've given up on Shibuya.

00:07:55.390 --> 00:07:57.890
So, I've decided to erase it.

00:07:57.890 --> 00:07:59.430
Please wait, sir!

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:02.850
Shibuya still holds so many possibilities!

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:08.480
But the senses of its denizens are so
dulled that they don't even notice.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:10.940
Shibuya exerts a powerful influence.

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:14.700
I have to act before ripples
spread to other districts.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:17.410
I swear, I will reform Shibuya!

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:18.830
How?

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:23.500
I'll find a way. So please!

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:27.420
Please give me a chance to save Shibuya!

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:29.710
Let's play a game.

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:30.920
A game, sir?

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:33.800
Yes. A game between us.

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:35.220
The rules are simple.

00:08:35.220 --> 00:08:37.970
If you can reform Shibuya,
Megumi, you win.

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:40.180
Shibuya will remain.

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:42.060
And if I fail?

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:43.440
I win.

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:46.560
I'll erase both you and Shibuya.

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:50.940
You have one month.

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:54.700
I don't care how you use it. Best of luck.

00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:03.750
For real?<i> You're </i>the Composer?!

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:08.340
I found his "reformed"
Shibuya a little intriguing.

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:09.590
Bastard!

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:13.880
Stop runnin' your mouth!

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:17.470
What?!

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:25.100
Shit! What'd you do?!

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:29.940
Sorry, but may I ask you
to stay out of this?

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:38.200
Shiki?! Beat?!

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:40.120
Wh-What's going on?!

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:43.950
I can't move!

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:45.040
Hey!

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:49.000
I won't damage your precious friends.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:50.790
--Still...
--The hell did you do?!

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:52.880
They are a bit noisy.

00:09:57.380 --> 00:10:02.310
As the Composer, my power was far more
powerful than Megumi's for fair play.

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:08.020
I sealed my natural powers and observed
the Underground from the Realground.

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:11.150
I decided to send someone to play for me.

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:15.150
A single proxy from the Realground.

00:10:15.150 --> 00:10:16.860
No way...

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:20.740
That's right, Neku: you.

00:10:20.740 --> 00:10:24.700
Then, everything...
everything I've done was...

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:29.120
Helping me to erase Shibuya.

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:35.210
Were you the one who beat Minamimoto too?

00:10:35.210 --> 00:10:41.180
Your battle with Megumi was sacred.
I couldn't have him interfering.

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:45.470
Besides, he did get in my way
when I went to welcome you.

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:46.770
What do you...?

00:10:48.190 --> 00:10:50.520
As a prize for winning the game,

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:54.690
I'll return your final missing memories.
I've been holding onto them,

00:10:54.690 --> 00:10:56.150
Neku.

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:15.150
It was <i>you</i>!

00:12:15.150 --> 00:12:17.570
<i>You </i>killed me!

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:19.230
I did.

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:25.200
All this time, I've been blaming
myself for not trusting you!

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:27.990
You made it look like it was Minamimoto!

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:31.870
He was angling to make
himself the Composer.

00:12:31.870 --> 00:12:36.130
It seems he believed he could
kill me in the Realground.

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:38.550
Obviously, he miscalculated.

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:48.510
You see, unlike the Reapers, the Composer
can wield some power in the Realground.

00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:52.390
After he fled back to the Underground,

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:56.860
he turned himself Taboo in an
effort to bridge the power gap.

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:05.820
I'd better punish Mr. Hanekoma too.
He should have stayed out of it.

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:10.240
Have you taken a liking to this room?

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:12.410
What do you mean?

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:15.290
Let's play a game.

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:21.260
The winner gets to become the Composer
and do with Shibuya as he pleases.

00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:26.050
If you win, Neku, you can make
the Shibuya of your dreams.

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:30.720
You can even restore your friends to life.
Not a bad deal, is it?

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:35.230
When the countdown reaches zero,
we fire our guns. That's all.

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:36.520
Simple, right?

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:42.990
Enough playing around.

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:45.280
I'm not playing around.

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:49.530
It may surprise you, but forks in
the road of life are just this simple.

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:52.120
Ten.

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:54.790
Nine.

00:13:56.460 --> 00:13:57.670
Eight.

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:00.210
Seven.

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:05.260
Six.

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:07.340
I will...

00:14:07.340 --> 00:14:08.550
Five.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:12.060
Four.

00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:15.140
Trust your partner.

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:17.060
Three.

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:22.230
I... I managed to make it this far
because I trusted everyone.

00:14:22.230 --> 00:14:23.480
Two.

00:14:27.110 --> 00:14:28.320
One.

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:35.580
I'll... trust you.

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:15.540
What? What's going on?!

00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:18.000
Is this Shibuya?

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:20.750
Oh, excuse me.

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:35.310
Shibuya's still here, and so am I.

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:41.650
Did I come back to life?

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:56.200
Yo!

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:57.950
Over here!

00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:02.880
Beat! Rhyme!

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:04.880
What took you so long?

00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:07.750
I almost thought you forgot our promise.

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:10.970
My bro's been waiting the whole time.

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:13.260
I have not!

00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:15.680
You got to come back to life, too!

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:18.890
You bet. No clue how, though.

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:22.690
I'm sure it's all thanks
to Neku, you, and Shiki.

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:25.810
Where's Shiki?

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:41.790
I'm Neku Sakuraba.

00:16:41.790 --> 00:16:43.670
Call me Neku.

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:47.090
I'm Shiki Misaki. Call me Shiki.

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:49.670
Shiki.

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:54.130
We got to see each other again, Neku.

00:16:59.140 --> 00:17:02.560
Well, for now,
everything's back to normal.

00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:06.940
This whole mess is going to
cause trouble with the higher ups.

00:17:06.940 --> 00:17:13.530
Allowing Kitaniji, a Reaper, to run
the game is totally unprecedented.

00:17:13.530 --> 00:17:20.080
You also fought alongside Neku
with your powers suppressed.

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:22.250
That was another shock.

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:25.750
Wasn't that a big risk?

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:31.590
Minamimoto figured out who you were
and tailed you in the Realground, right?

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:36.430
I'm the Composer. No Reaper can kill me.

00:17:36.430 --> 00:17:43.730
But Minamimoto knew what I look like in
the Realground. Not even Megumi knew that.

00:17:43.730 --> 00:17:46.900
I don't suppose you told him?

00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:53.490
What makes you think that?

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:57.110
You also wanted to preserve Shibuya.

00:17:57.110 --> 00:17:58.820
The Red Skull pins.

00:17:58.820 --> 00:18:00.950
Whoa.

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:05.290
Megumi asked you to make them for him.

00:18:05.290 --> 00:18:09.000
Yes. It was a request from
the acting Composer.

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:11.710
It's not like I broke any rules.

00:18:11.710 --> 00:18:16.180
These pins are for imprinting
Kitaniji's will on people.

00:18:17.630 --> 00:18:23.930
It was a good idea, but he could only
imprint on humans wearing the pins.

00:18:23.930 --> 00:18:30.610
That's why Kitaniji used missions as
a cover to distribute Red Skull pins.

00:18:30.610 --> 00:18:32.860
I guess that's abuse of authority.

00:18:34.990 --> 00:18:40.160
Oh yeah, I heard there's
new graffiti in Udagawa.

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:42.410
They say it showed up overnight.

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:44.330
Everyone's talking about it.

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:45.910
It's Mr. Hanekoma.

00:18:47.750 --> 00:18:49.880
What're you grinnin' about?

00:18:49.880 --> 00:18:51.710
I'm not grinning.

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:52.040
--You can't wait to go check it out, right?

00:18:52.040 --> 00:18:55.300
--There's a reason I painted
graffiti all over Shibuya.
--You can't wait to go check it out, right?

00:18:55.300 --> 00:18:57.300
--There's a reason I painted
graffiti all over Shibuya.
--Well, yeah.

00:18:57.300 --> 00:19:01.010
Graffiti isn't limited to a select few;

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:05.430
it lets me imprint on all the humans
who come in contact with it.

00:19:07.560 --> 00:19:12.610
All my graffiti is infused with
code for a certain command.

00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:16.190
"Enjoy every moment with all you've got"?

00:19:16.190 --> 00:19:18.150
I'm surprised you knew.

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:21.700
Neku was happy to tell me about it.

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:24.620
He's the one I had the most influence on.

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:28.790
Why didn't you erase Shibuya?

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:32.250
Because of Neku.

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:34.170
He'd chosen to shut his ears,

00:19:34.170 --> 00:19:38.800
not believe anything anyone said,
and live his life alone.

00:19:38.800 --> 00:19:42.010
But he trusted me and lowered his gun.

00:19:42.010 --> 00:19:45.720
That's all there was to it.

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:50.560
He changed dramatically over the
course of his three Reapers' Games.

00:19:50.560 --> 00:19:52.690
It's a minor miracle.

00:19:58.110 --> 00:20:03.570
Still, how come we were able
to pull off a killer move like that?

00:20:03.570 --> 00:20:09.250
I had a feeling that CAT--
Mr. Hanekoma--was cheering us on.

00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:11.920
That pin with his letter...

00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:14.630
That wasn't a keypin, was it?

00:20:14.630 --> 00:20:16.590
Was that really fair?

00:20:16.590 --> 00:20:20.220
Hey, you gave him a special
pin disguised as a Player Pin

00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:23.390
so that Kitaniji's brainwashing
wouldn't work on him.

00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:25.510
I'd say we're even.

00:20:25.510 --> 00:20:27.560
I'll let it slide,

00:20:27.560 --> 00:20:32.730
but in exchange, may I ask why you
tampered with Minamimoto's Refinery?

00:20:32.730 --> 00:20:37.190
I had high hopes for Minamimoto's
attachment to Shibuya.

00:20:37.190 --> 00:20:42.650
He was one way Shibuya might
survive after Kitaniji lost.

00:20:43.740 --> 00:20:49.330
You wanted to have him defeat me
and become the new Composer?

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:52.250
I'm fully prepared to fall from grace.

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:53.500
Of course.

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:58.500
Still, your words spurred
on Neku's metamorphosis,

00:21:02.670 --> 00:21:04.590
--It's been ages, huh?
--as did my starting the
Reapers' Game with Megumi,

00:21:04.590 --> 00:21:06.180
--as did my starting the
Reapers' Game with Megumi,

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:06.680
--Nekky!
--as did my starting the
Reapers' Game with Megumi,

00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:08.260
--Nekky!
--your turning Minamimoto Taboo,
even at the risk of falling,

00:21:08.260 --> 00:21:10.890
--your turning Minamimoto Taboo,
even at the risk of falling,

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:11.230
--Hey!
--your turning Minamimoto Taboo,
even at the risk of falling,

00:21:11.230 --> 00:21:11.890
--Hey!
--and Neku's encounters with other Players.

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:13.230
--You guys!
--and Neku's encounters with other Players.

00:21:13.230 --> 00:21:14.810
--You're alive again.
--and Neku's encounters with other Players.

00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:16.900
--Finally! I've been dying for one of these.
--and Neku's encounters with other Players.

00:21:16.900 --> 00:21:19.940
--Finally! I've been dying for one of these.
--Perhaps that means it was all necessary.

00:21:21.190 --> 00:21:22.190
--Looks like you're all fired up today!

00:21:22.190 --> 00:21:23.450
--I guess so.
--Looks like you're all fired up today!

00:21:23.450 --> 00:21:26.870
Try to keep up! Let's rock!

00:21:28.910 --> 00:21:34.670
They proved that nothing
in this world is pointless.

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:42.340
So, "enjoy every moment"?

00:21:44.010 --> 00:21:47.430
What's up? You sound kind of lonely.

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:53.810
Good grief. He always puts up a front.

00:21:58.520 --> 00:22:02.190
It's a wonderful world, huh?
